    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense from a systemic view, but I'm trying to refine the predictive accuracy of the model. If we were to implement a patrol strategy based strictly on these risk assessments, wouldn't the model essentially be recommending a disproportionate police presence in Black neighborhoods due to these historical correlations? In a real-world deployment, how would the model distinguish between \"preventative presence\" and \"racial profiling\" if the data inputs themselves are so heavily tied to race?",
